    "text": "IF polygraphs were actually reliable, they'd be admissible in court. Even if part of a cadre of 'evidence'. DECADES of research has shown that a law-abiding citizen, let alone one in the midst of GRIEF/ANXIETY, will have physiological responses that skew data. The expert featured here, does allude to such, but honest to goodness, we've FAR more sophisticated technology now, than when 'polygraphs/lie detectors' were first brought to market.",
